  message: "FIXED, PR #1248 (dev 3352f6af59).\n\nWHAT CHANGED\n- record_declaration is an enclosing type. A record is a `record` symbol (the registered kind names Java 14+), emitted by one table-driven arm now shared with class and interface.\n- Components are emitted as private final fields, through one _java_field_symbol helper that the field arm also uses.\n- compact_constructor_declaration is a constructor, and its signature is the record's components. The java DDG walks it.\n- The three class/interface/enum kind filters now derive from one set, so records reach class_symbols and `new R(..)` resolves to an `instantiates` edge.\n- The containment linker treats `record` as a container.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE\n- test_java_records.py on the production analyzer: the filed repro (a record with methods and a static factory) now yields the record, its fields, both constructor forms with signatures, its methods, and a nested record. Calls anchor on the record's members.\n- The jenkins shape (Outer.kill plus a nested record's kill) now yields two distinct symbols.\n- A/B surveys against dev cc3a7cabf7 (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pidos_09272026/RESULT.md):\n\n  | repo | records | instantiates |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | trino | 836 | +4,480 |\n  | kafka | 258 | +1,348 |\n  | spring-boot | 137 | +226 |\n  | jenkins | 10 | +8 |\n\n- Calls fall on trino (-2,942) and kafka (-85). Every lost trino edge was classified:\n  - 3,624 went into record members that were misnamed onto the outer class, which picked up unrelated toString/id/add calls. These were wrong edges.\n  - 164 were calls bound to a same-named class in another module by the inherited_calls type fallback. Example: DropColumnTask -> the hive plugin's TableMetadata class, where trino-main's TableMetadata is a record. Also wrong edges.\n  - The rest re-anchor onto the record or its constructor, or resolve to a better target, e.g. QueryId.valueOf now reaches trino's own QueryId record.\n  - 2 are unclassified.\n\nNOT DONE, stated\n- A record's implicit accessors (r.a()) are not emitted as methods.\n- A bare call from a nested type to its outer type's method is unresolved. This holds for nested classes too, so it is not record-specific.\n- JEP 512 compact source files (a top-level `void main()`) emit no symbol; java_callable_name returns None for them, and the DDG naming test pins that the DDG skips them."  # 0b39
